Jetmir counts your creatures. With three, every creature you control gets +1/+0 and vigilance; with six, +2/+0 and trample as well; with nine, +3/+0 and double strike too. At nine, a 1/1 Goblin token is a 4/1 with double strike and trample — 8 damage — and ten of them are 80. Vigilance keeps your attackers untapped to block afterwards, so attack every turn.
And any infinite loop of hasty creatures with Jetmir out is an unlimited army of double strikers — the deck has several — see the combos.
Mana creatures count toward the thresholds, and so do tokens made at instant speed. Secure the Wastes or March of the Multitudes after blockers are declared can take you from six creatures to nine before damage. The bonuses also drop the moment you fall below a threshold, so don't trade creatures away mid-combat when you're sitting on exactly nine.

# The commander
Jetmir, Nexus of Revels :: four mana. Three creatures: +1/+0 and vigilance. Six: also +1/+0 and trample. Nine: also +1/+0 and double strike. Every creature you control, tokens included.
Lightning Greaves :: shroud the turn Jetmir lands — the table knows what it does. Never equip it to Kiki-Jiki — shroud stops Zealous Conscripts or Restoration Angel from targeting Kiki.

# Infinite combos — why this is Bracket 3.5
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Zealous Conscripts :: Kiki copies Conscripts, and the copy's enter trigger untaps Kiki — target Kiki itself. Repeat for as many hasty 3/3s as you want, the same turn Kiki lands (it has haste). With Jetmir out every copy is a double striker; Impact Tremors and General Kreat turn them into damage before they even attack. Never leave Lightning Greaves on Kiki: shroud stops the Conscripts copy targeting it.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Restoration Angel :: Kiki copies the Angel; the copy blinks Kiki, which comes back untapped with haste. Flash: start it in an opponent's end step and the copies last until the end of your next turn.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Village Bell-Ringer :: the copy untaps every creature you control, Kiki included. Flash, so this one works in an opponent's end step too.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Lightning Crafter + Goblin Bombardment :: Kiki copies the Crafter. The copy's champion trigger exiles Kiki; the hasty copy taps for 3 damage; sacrifice it to Goblin Bombardment; Kiki returns untapped — it has haste — and copies the Crafter again. Unlimited 3-damage shots, so this one kills on its own. The original Crafter must stay on the battlefield; when it enters you must exile another Goblin or Shaman (champion) or sacrifice it.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Thornbite Staff + Goblin Bombardment :: the Staff attaches itself to Kiki when Kiki enters after it (otherwise equip costs {4}). Kiki copies any nonlegendary creature, you sacrifice a creature to Goblin Bombardment, and the death untaps Kiki. Unlimited loops. This loop deals damage rather than building an army.
Krenko, Mob Boss + Thornbite Staff + Goblin Bombardment :: equip the Staff to Krenko ({4} — he's a Warrior, so it won't attach itself). Krenko taps for a Goblin per Goblin; sacrifice one to Goblin Bombardment; the death untaps Krenko; tap again. The army doubles every lap. Win with Impact Tremors, General Kreat or a double-striking attack.

# Tutor lines — what to fetch, and when
Goblin Matron -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: when you already hold Zealous Conscripts, Restoration Angel, Village Bell-Ringer, Lightning Crafter or the Staff — Kiki is the piece that turns half a combo into a kill.
Goblin Matron -> Goblin Recruiter :: when you're missing two or more pieces. Matron gets Recruiter; Recruiter stacks the rest on top of your library.
Goblin Matron -> Krenko, Mob Boss :: when Thornbite Staff is already out, or when you simply need a board this turn.
Goblin Matron -> Lightning Crafter :: when Kiki-Jiki is on the battlefield and you have a free outlet — the Crafter is the last piece.
Imperial Recruiter -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: power 2, so the one non-Goblin tutor that still finds Kiki. It also gets Village Bell-Ringer or Goblin Recruiter.
Eladamri's Call -> Zealous Conscripts :: instant speed, for the non-Goblin half that Matron can't find.
Chord of Calling -> Restoration Angel :: with Kiki already out, Chord the Angel in at the end of an opponent's turn and go off right there. Convoke lets your army pay the generic part.
Formidable Speaker -> Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: discard a spare card when it enters to find any creature — Kiki, or whichever partner you lack.
Goblin Recruiter -> Goblin Ringleader + Muxus, Goblin Grandee :: choose a four-card hand refill or a six-creature deployment. The exact piles and draw sequencing are below; either payoff works without the commander.

# Goblin Recruiter setups — what to stack, top card first
Goblin Recruiter -> Goblin Ringleader :: TOP to BOTTOM: Goblin Ringleader; Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker; Lightning Crafter; Skirk Prospector; Goblin Warchief. Draw or otherwise reach Ringleader, then cast it: its entry trigger puts the next four selected Goblins into your hand. Those creatures still need to be cast; Ringleader does not deploy them. If Ringleader is already in hand, start the pile with the four targets instead.
Goblin Recruiter -> Muxus, Goblin Grandee :: TOP to BOTTOM: Muxus, Goblin Grandee; Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker; Lightning Crafter; Skirk Prospector; Goblin Warchief; Goblin Ringleader; Krenko, Mob Boss. Reach and cast Muxus; all six following cards are Goblin creatures with mana value five or less, so its entry trigger puts them onto the battlefield. If Muxus is already in hand, omit it from the pile and reveal the six immediately.
Goblin Ringleader :: Put these four cards immediately UNDER the six-card Muxus package: Goblin Matron; Siege-Gang Commander; Goblin Chieftain; Howlsquad Heavy. When Muxus deploys Ringleader, the entry trigger puts this backup package into your hand. Resolve Ringleader before any other draw triggers and before the original Lightning Crafter's champion trigger. Only stack cards still in your library; substitute useful Goblins for pieces already in hand or on the battlefield.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker + Lightning Crafter + Skirk Prospector :: The original Crafter champions the Recruiter that made the pile, or the Ringleader AFTER its refill resolves. Keep Kiki and Prospector on the battlefield. Tap Kiki to copy Crafter; the hasty copy champions Kiki, taps for 3 damage, then is sacrificed to Prospector for {R}. Kiki returns untapped with haste. Repeat for lethal damage and red mana. No combat or commander is required, but removal or effects that stop the entry triggers/activated abilities can interrupt it.
Goblin Warchief :: Included on the Muxus board to give your other Goblins haste and reduce the generic cost of backup Goblin spells. Kiki and its copies already have haste; Warchief is for Krenko and the wider recovery plan.
Use the next natural draw to reach the payoff, or arrange for an existing draw engine to take exactly the intended cards. If Skullclamp will draw two, put an extra useful Goblin above the payoff so the four/six-card package stays intact.
Guardian Project :: Order the Muxus entry trigger ABOVE Project's draw trigger so Muxus reveals its intended six first. When those creatures enter, put Ringleader's trigger above their Project draws so it gets the intended four. Mandatory draws also limit how many Kiki loops you can safely repeat; finish before your library empties.
Searches that shuffle undo the pile: use fetch lands and other tutors BEFORE Recruiter. Any extra draw, mill or exile also changes the positions; account for it before committing. Muxus only puts eligible Goblin CREATURES onto the battlefield: Goblin-typed instants/enchantments and Muxus itself are not hits. Recruiter does not put the payoff in your hand for free.

# Getting to nine
Krenko, Mob Boss :: taps for a 1/1 per Goblin you control. Thanks to vigilance it can attack AND tap afterwards.
Krenko, Tin Street Kingpin :: each attack puts a +1/+1 counter on it, then makes Goblins equal to its power — two the first time, three the next.
Siege-Gang Commander :: four creatures from one card.
Mogg War Marshal :: two creatures, and another when it dies.
Legion Warboss :: a hasty Goblin each of your combats.
Goblin Rabblemaster :: a hasty Goblin every combat. Your other Goblins must attack, which costs nothing with Jetmir's vigilance.
Siege-Gang Lieutenant :: two hasty Goblins each of your combats while Jetmir is on the battlefield.
Howlsquad Heavy :: a Goblin each of your combats, and haste for every other Goblin.
General Kreat, the Boltbringer :: a Goblin when your Goblins attack, and 1 damage to each opponent per other creature that enters.
Ainok Strike Leader :: whenever it or Jetmir attacks, a 1/1 Goblin attacking each opponent.
Kiki-Jiki, Mirror Breaker :: a hasty copy each turn — Siege-Gang Commander is four more creatures every turn.
Fable of the Mirror-Breaker :: a Goblin that makes Treasure when it attacks, then a card filter, then Reflection of Kiki-Jiki — a copy maker that costs {1} each use and needs a turn before it can tap.
Secure the Wastes :: X 1/1s at instant speed — the cheapest way to jump to nine mid-combat.
March of the Multitudes :: X lifelink 1/1s at instant speed, and convoke lets your creatures pay for it.

# Haste
Goblin Chieftain :: other Goblins +1/+1 and haste.
Goblin Warchief :: Goblins cost one less and have haste.
The Fire Crystal :: every creature you control has haste, and red spells cost one less.
Rhythm of the Wild :: your creature spells can't be countered, and nontoken creatures enter with haste or a +1/+1 counter.

# Making it lethal
Shared Animosity :: every attacking Goblin gets +1/+0 for each other attacking Goblin — and double strike hits with all of it twice.
Warleader's Call :: your creatures get +1/+1, and every creature that enters deals 1 to each opponent.
Beastmaster Ascension :: one counter per attacker; at seven your creatures get +5/+5. One attack turns it on for good.
Akroma's Will :: with Jetmir out, both modes: flying and double strike, plus lifelink, indestructible and protection from every colour.
Kessig Wolf Run :: pump one attacker and give it trample.
Castle Embereth :: {1}{R}{R} and a tap: your creatures get +1/+0.

# Damage on the side
Impact Tremors :: 1 to each opponent for every creature that enters.
Goblin Bombardment :: sacrifice a creature for 1 damage anywhere. Careful not to drop below nine mid-combat.

# Mana
Skirk Prospector :: sacrifice a Goblin for {R}. A one-mana creature for Jetmir's thresholds, acceleration for Muxus, and the free outlet Recruiter can find for the Crafter combo. Preserve your creature count when winning through combat.
Gaea's Cradle :: a green mana for every creature you control.
Circle of Dreams Druid :: the same on a creature.
Birds of Paradise :: a one-mana source of any colour.
Llanowar Elves :: a one-mana green source.
Elvish Mystic :: the same.
Avacyn's Pilgrim :: a one-mana white source.
Nature's Lore :: a Forest dual onto the battlefield.
Three Visits :: the same.
Sol Ring :: the fastest start.
Arcane Signet :: any of your three colours.
Jeska's Will :: with Jetmir out, both halves: a red mana for each card in an opponent's hand, and the top three cards to play this turn.
Three Tree City :: name Goblin: {2} and a tap make a mana for every Goblin you control.
Cavern of Souls :: name Goblin: they can't be countered.

# Cards
Skullclamp :: equip it to a creature with 1 toughness and it dies: two cards for one mana. A lord that adds toughness keeps your tokens alive, so pick an X/1.
Guardian Project :: a card whenever a nontoken creature with a new name enters.
Tocasia's Welcome :: a card once a turn when a creature with mana value 3 or less enters — tokens count.
Sylvan Library :: see three cards every turn.
Esper Sentinel :: taxes each opponent's first noncreature spell each turn or draws you a card.

# Protection
Teferi's Protection :: the whole board phases out until your next turn.
Heroic Intervention :: hexproof and indestructible for everything.
Flawless Maneuver :: free with Jetmir out; your creatures become indestructible.
Clever Concealment :: phase out any of your nonland permanents; convoke lets your tokens pay.
Boros Charm :: indestructible for everything, double strike for one creature, or 4 damage to a player.
Silence :: one mana and nobody else casts spells this turn. Cast it before you start a combo.
Voice of Victory :: your opponents can't cast spells during your turn, and it brings two attacking Warriors when it attacks.

# Answers
Swords to Plowshares :: one mana, any creature.
Path to Exile :: the second one.
Beast Within :: any permanent; they get a 3/3.
Generous Gift :: the same, in white.
Chaos Warp :: the red answer to anything.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep a mana creature and something that makes two bodies. Cast Jetmir on turn three or four with three creatures already out and your team attacks for real at once.
Attack every turn — vigilance means the army is still there to block.
Count before combat. Eight creatures and an instant token spell in hand is nine with double strike.
